[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Kghaffari26/sam-agent/pulls/2","id":4895036605,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUolC4c8AAAABI8RUvQ","html_url":"https://github.com/Kghaffari26/sam-agent/pull/2","diff_url":"https://github.com/Kghaffari26/sam-agent/pull/2.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Kghaffari26/sam-agent/pull/2.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Kghaffari26/sam-agent/issues/2","number":2,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Next round: judge calibration and label review tooling, live research audit and fixes, email alerts","user":{"login":"Kghaffari26","id":108359594,"node_id":"U_kgDOBnVvqg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108359594?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26","html_url":"https://github.com/Kghaffari26","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kghaffari26/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Scope: `docs/specs/SCOPE_SAM_AGENT_NEXT.md` (S1–S4). S3 and S4 are done; S1 and S2 are built and wait on the owner's scores and label review.\n\n## S3: live bid research audit and fixes\n`scripts/audit_research.py` re-fetches every claim in the published briefs from USAspending.gov and SAM.gov. It runs as the new **Audit - Research** workflow (`workflow_dispatch`), because neither host is reachable from the dev container. Report: `docs/research_audit_2026-10.md`.\n\n- Every concrete claim in the 5 live briefs matched its source: award ids, amounts, agency, NAICS, attachments and dollar figures.\n- **Fixed at the cause**, each with a regression test built from the real response:\n  - **Sub-agency sent as a toptier agency.** Navy, NOAA, FEMA and DHA were sent to USAspending as toptier agencies, which matched nothing, so 4 briefs said \"no prior awards\". They now go out as subtier filters (`usaspending.awarding_agency_filter`).\n  - **Empty searches.** An empty search now falls back to the notice's agency and NAICS code without keywords.\n  - **Keywords as one string.** A `keywords` string is now accepted instead of failing validation.\n  - **Leaked tool-call markup.** Leaked `<parameter name=…>` markup in the `finish` call had emptied one brief's prior awards. The parameters are now repaired back into their fields, and the guard rejects any markup left in the text.\n- Research prompt v1 → v2. Re-researched with the fixes, all 5 briefs pass every check and name the real incumbents. Research eval on v2: pass rate 1.00, every check 1.00 (including `required_tools`, which was 0.90), judge 0.95.\n- The audit used 0 SAM.gov requests.\n\n## S4: email alert digest\n- `[alerts]` in `config/grants.toml` and `agents/grants/alerts.py` send one digest per run of strong new matches: fit ≥ 80, Pursue, at most 5 a day.\n- Nothing repeats: what was sent is recorded by notice id + content hash in `data/grants/alerts.json`.\n- Plain text plus simple HTML, sent through Resend.\n- Sent by a new `alerts` job in `agent-grants.yml` after a successful run.\n- Missing secrets or a delivery error never fail the run; the next run adds a `meta.warnings` line.\n- `--dry-run` (and the workflow input `alerts_dry_run`) writes the digest to the job summary instead of sending it.\n\n## S1 / S2: ready for the owner\n- **S1:** `scripts/make_calibration_sheet.py` freezes 20 items (`evals/grants/calibration/`). Once they're scored by hand, `scripts/calibrate_judges.py` reports Spearman's ρ, MAE and a threshold mapping, and the suites take calibrated pass thresholds from `calibration.json`.\n- **S2:** `scripts/review_labels.py` builds `labels_review.md` (the model's disagreements first, `r3-nsf-grant` at the top). `--apply` writes `labels_reviewed.json`, and the scoring suite switches to it.\n- `scripts/import_review.py` brings in answers from the private review page.\n\n## Checks\n- 289 tests pass; ruff and actionlint are clean.\n- Round spend $0.64 of the $3.00 cap.\n- The Evals PR gate will re-run all three suites. Research v2's baseline is already in `evals/history.jsonl`.\n\n## After merge (owner)\n- Add the secrets `ALERT_EMAIL_API_KEY` and `ALERT_EMAIL_TO`.\n- Run \"Agent - Grants\" by hand twice: the first run should send the digest, the second should send nothing new.\n\nGaps noted under \"Needed from agents-core\" in `STATUS.md`:\n- extra secrets / a post-run hook in `run-agent.yml`\n- Spearman and calibration history in evals\n- repair of leaked tool-call parameters in `agent_loop`\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01TPgNR48a91Apqy3xCftky4)_","created_at":"2026-10-16T22:33:07Z","updated_at":"2026-10-16T22:33:07Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"b5f2e4fb6a4dbe35149c5400dc15f71d9a42fb8c","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Kghaffari26/sam-agent/pulls/2/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Kghaffari26/sam-agent/pulls/2/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Kghaffari26/sam-agent/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Kghaffari26/sam-agent/issues/2/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Kghaffari26/sam-agent/statuses/5a9dbeda0b060bf186549ece5a6050384b5b62c9","head":{"label":"Kghaffari26:claude/vibrant-cori-nuwdi6","ref":"claude/vibrant-cori-nuwdi6","sha":"5a9dbeda0b060bf186